  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A rectangular sheet of fixed perimeter with sides having their lengths in the ratio <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>15</mn></math>&nbsp;is converted into an open rectangular box&nbsp;by folding after removing squares of equal area from all four corners. If the total area of removed squares is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn></math>, the resulting box has maximum volume. Then the lengths of the sides of the rectangular sheet are:</p>",
    "image": null
  },
